-----------------------------------------------------------------------------



         Setup commands used in the BBS:CONFS/(conf)/DIR_ULFILES
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
A little information about the ULPATH / DLPATH commands.
You can have as many as you like of both ULPATH and the DLPATH in the
setup file.
For DLPATH, File will be traced/located in the order you setup the list.
For ULPATH, system will select first available drivepath which got
enough free space for uploading.


CORRUPTFILES             (pt)   : DEFAULT: BBS:CONFS/(conf)/HOLD/
                                : Select an alternative path to put private
                                  or currupt files.
                                  If you have created a HOLD directory in
                                  the conference where it is possible to
                                  upload files. This specified directory
                                  path got second priority.

DLPATH                   (pt)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : a full path , where a user can download
                                  files from.
                                  This is the path where files in the
                                  dirlistings should be available from.

ULPATH                   (pt)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : a full path , where uploaded files will be
                                  moved to.
                                  NOTE: for users to be able to download the
                                        uploaded files, without the sysop
                                        moving files to another directory,
                                        specify this path as DLPATH too.


-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
         Setup commands used in the BBS:CONFS/(conf)/DIRECTORIES
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

DIRS                     (pn)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : number of directory listings available

NAMEDIR(n)               (pt)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : Alternative name for dirlistings file
                                  default name is DIR1,DIR2,... etc...


-----------------------------------------------------------------------------
                 Setup commands used in the CONF.CFG
-----------------------------------------------------------------------------

FORCE_NEWSCAN(n)                : DEFAULT: OFF
                                : Force newmailscan when joining a
                                  conference, ignoring users selection.

FILEBASE(n)                     : DEFAULT: OFF
                                : This conference will only be used for files

FREEDOWNLOAD(n)                 : DEFAULT: OFF
                                : Files in this conference are free download.
                                  user will not be credited for downloading
                                  in the conference.

FORCEPRIVATE(n)                 : DEFAULT: OFF
                                : Force all mail written, as private.
                                  to be used with NetMail conferences.

FORCEPUBLIC(n)                  : DEFAULT: OFF
                                : Force all mail written, as public.
                                  to be used with NetMail conferences.


KEEPMAIL_READ(n)         (pn)   : DEFAULT: OFF
                                : Number of days to keep mail which is not
                                  deleted and is received by user.

KEEPMAIL_UNREAD(n)       (pn)   : DEFAULT: OFF
                                : Number of days to keep mail which is not
                                  deleted and is still not received by user.
                                  this also includes ALL messages.

LVLACCESS_CONF(n)        (pn)   : DEFAULT: OFF
                                : Select minimum accesslevel needed for
                                  accessing this conference

MESSAGEBASE(n)                  : DEFAULT: OFF
                                : This conference will only be used as
                                  messagbase.

NAME_CONF(n)             (pt)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : name of conference

NO_NEWSCAN(n)                   : DEFAULT: OFF
                                : Skip newmailscan in conference ignoring
                                  users selection.

PASSWORD_CONF(n)         (pt)   : DEFAULT: OFF
                                : Password for entering conference.
                                  If password is used, user will be prompted
                                  for a password when he tries to join
                                  this conference.

PATHNAME_CONF(n)         (pt)   : DEFAULT: OFF
                                : Pathname to conference directory.
                                  This is only the directory name of the
                                  conference and NOT the FULL PATH.
                                  i.e. BBS:CONFS/(pathname_conf)/
                                  path_name_conf%1 could be NEWUSER
                                  and full path to directory is then
                                  BBS:CONFS/NEWUSER/

SYSOPMAILCONF(n)         (pn)   : NO DEFAULT
                                : Alternative conference to save comments to
                                  sysop in.

SHOW_NEW_FILES(n)               : DEFAULT: OFF
                                : Force newfiles scan when joining conference
                                  ignoring users selection.

USERTYPE_CONF(n)         (pt)   : DEFAULT: OFF
                                : Select a specific usertype that can enter
                                  this conference.
                                  This is just an alternative to the specified
                                  conference available, used in USERTYPE.
                                  Entering a usertype here, will grant access
                                  to conference ignoring usertype.

USESENTBY(n)                    : DEFAULT: OFF
                                : Use "Sent by:" signature lines in
                                  dirlistings.
